[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains utility templates for generating reStructuredText
(RST) documentation and PlantUML context diagrams from UML models.

PlantUML diagram templates:
  pu_classDiagram     - Context diagram for a UML class, showing
                        associated classes, super/sub classes,
                        associations, and abstraction relationships.
  pu_dataTypeDiagram  - Context diagram for a UML data type, showing
                        classes and data types that use the type,
                        the dotted usage connection, and the
                        inheritance hierarchy.
  pu_superClass       - Helper: renders superclass nodes and their
                        limited inherited associations for pu_classDiagram.
  pu_subClasses       - Helper: renders subclass inheritance arrows
                        recursively for pu_classDiagram.
  pu_superDataType    - Helper: renders supertype inheritance for
                        pu_dataTypeDiagram.
  pu_subDataTypes     - Helper: renders subtype inheritance for
                        pu_dataTypeDiagram.

RST documentation templates:
  rst_mainIndexHead            - Index page header and toctree.
  rst_generationMessageDoc     - Generation message comment.
  rst_header                   - Section header underline.
  rst_classOrDataTypeInheritance - Collapsible inheritance tree.
  rst_subClasses               - Recursive subclass list.
  rst_processAttributeInTable  - Table row for a class attribute.
  rst_processAssociationInTable - Table row for an association.
  rst_refDataType              - RST :ref: link for a type.
  rst_simpleQualifiedClassNameReference     - :ref: for a class.
  rst_simpleQualifiedClassifierNameReference - :ref: for a classifier.
  rst_classNameReference       - :ref: for a class by qualified name.
  rst_classifierNameReference  - :ref: for a classifier by qualified name.
  rst_className                - Class name with italic for abstract.
  rst_addClassReferencesToDocumentation - Injects :ref: links into
                                          documentation strings.
  abstractionType              - UML abstraction stereotype label.

HTML diagram modal templates:
  diagramModalPreCode   - Opening tags for the SVG diagram modal.
  diagramModalPostCode  - Closing tags and modal controls.

Indentation utilities:
  e_indent  - Post-processor: prefixes every non-empty line with
              a fixed number of spaces (used for RST include blocks).
  e_indent2 - Post-processor: inserts indentation after each newline.
/]
[module rstUtilityDoc('http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types', 'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML', 'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard')/]

[import ucmism2t::queries::associationQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::classifierQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::classQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::configurationQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::dataTypeQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::elementQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::modelQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::packageQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::propertyQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::stringQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::typeQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::services::PropertiesService /]
[import ucmism2t::templates::target::doc::puDiagram/]
[import ucmism2t::templates::target::doc::puUtilityDoc/]

[**
Generates the main index page header for the RST field-level
documentation, including the model comment body and the root
toctree directive.

@param aModel - The UML model being documented.
/]
[template public rst_mainIndexHead(aModel : uml::Model)]
  Field-Level Documentation
  *************************
  
  .. raw:: html
  
     <hr/>
  
  [aModel.u_commentBody().replaceAll('(=\\s)', '$1\r')/]
  
  -----
  
  .. toctree::
     :hidden:

[/template]

[**
Generates the RST generation message comment, embedded at the top
of each generated RST file.

@param aNamedElement - The named element the file is generated for.
/]
[template public rst_generationMessageDoc(aNamedElement : uml::NamedElement)]
  .. This code was generated by the Eclipse Acceleo project UCMIS M2T.
     Target language is 'reStructuredText' ('doc') generated on the basis of the model '[aNamedElement.u_model().name/]'.

[/template]

[**
Generates a reStructuredText section header by repeating the
headerCharacter below the section title string.

@param aString          - The section title.
@param headerCharacter  - The underline character (=, -, ~, etc.).
/]
[template public rst_header(aString : String, headerCharacter : String)]
  [aString/]
  [headerCharacter.u_repeatChar(aString.size())/][/template]

[comment]
Working in Acceleo 3.7 — kept for reference:
[template public rst_header(aString : String, headerCharacter : String ) ]
[aString/]
[for (i : Integer | Sequence{1..aString.size()} ) ][headerCharacter/][/for]
[/template]
[/comment]

[**
Generates a PlantUML context diagram for a UML class.

The diagram shows:
  - The focal class (highlighted) with its own attributes
  - Associated classes grouped into three sections:
      (a) direct associated classes that are not superclasses,
          grouped in a 'together' block for Graphviz layout
      (b) abstraction supplier classes in a 'together' block
      (c) remaining context classes
  - Association arrows for the focal class
  - Superclass hierarchy (via pu_superClass) with limited
    inherited associations (max 3 per superclass)
  - Subclass hierarchy (via pu_subClasses)
  - Abstraction relationships when includeAllItems is true

All sections are subject to subset filtering via
u_isAssociationInSubset (for associations) and
u_profileSubsetClasses (for class nodes) when 'profiles' is true.

The diagram is @enduml-terminated and output as a complete
standalone PlantUML file.

@param aClass        - The UML class for which the context diagram
                        is generated.
@param aSubsetPackage - The profile sub-package whose dependency
                        relationships define the active subset, or
                        null for universe (no profile filtering).
/]
[template public pu_classDiagram(aClass : uml::Class, aSubsetPackage : uml::Package)]
  @startuml
  [aClass.pu_generationMessageDoc()/]
  !pragma ratio 0.5625
  [aClass.pu_options()/]
  
  title UML Diagram: Class [aClass.name/] in Context\n
  [let url : String = '../' + aClass.u_path() + '.html']
    [let label : String =
        aClass.u_model().u_modelTitle()
        + ' (' + aClass.u_model().u_modelAcronym() + ') '
        + aClass.u_model().u_modelMajorVersion()
        + '.' + aClass.u_model().u_modelMinorVersion()
        + ' - ' + aClass.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()]
      <style>
      title { FontSize: 20 }
      footer { hyperlinkUnderlineThickness 0 }
      </style>
      footer \n\n[url.pu_linkWithLabel(label)/]
      
    [/let]
  [/let]
  
  [if (aClass.u_allSuperClasses()->notEmpty() or aClass.u_allSubClasses()->notEmpty())]
    legend top left
    **Hint**
    <color:grey>- The arrows of the inheritance tree are <color:['uml-diagram-inheritance-arrow-color'.getPropertyValue()/]>colored<color:grey>.
    endlegend
  [/if]
  
  ' Core class of diagram
  [if (aClass.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [aClass.pu_classifierNameWithLabel('black', '<size:10>' + aClass.package.name + ':\\n')/] ['uml-diagram-class-emphasis-color'.getPropertyValue()/] {
  [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | aClass.ownedAttribute->select(temp1 | temp1.association = null)
    ->select(a | (aSubsetPackage <> null and a.u_isAttributeInProfile(aClass, aSubsetPackage)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and (aClass.name.u_subsetClassAttributes()->includes(a.name) or 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())))
    ->sortedBy(a | a.name))]
      [anAttribute.name/] : [anAttribute.type.pu_typeWithLink()/]
  [/for]
  }
  
  ' Associated classes without superclass.
  ' Placed in a 'together' block to reduce Graphviz layout constraints.
  [let directAssocClasses : OrderedSet(uml::Class) =
      aClass.u_associatedClasses() - aClass.superClass
        ->sortedBy(temp2 | temp2.package.name)
        ->sortedBy(temp3 | temp3.name)]
    [if (directAssocClasses->select(c | (aSubsetPackage <> null and aSubsetPackage.u_childDependencySupplierClasses()->includes(c)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue()))->notEmpty())]
      together {
      [for (contextClass : uml::Class | directAssocClasses)]
        [let inSubset1 : Boolean = (aSubsetPackage <> null and aSubsetPackage.u_childDependencySupplierClasses()->includes(contextClass)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())]
          [if (inSubset1)][if (contextClass.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [contextClass.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10>' + contextClass.package.name + ':\\n')/][/if]
        [/let]
      [/for]
      }
    [/if]
  [/let]
  
  ' Abstraction supplier classes.
  [let abstractionSuppliers : OrderedSet(uml::Class) =
      aClass.eInverse(uml::Abstraction)->asSequence()
        ->collect(temp4 | temp4.supplier)
        ->collect(temp5 | temp5.oclAsType(uml::Class))
        ->sortedBy(temp6 | temp6.package.name)
        ->sortedBy(temp7 | temp7.name)
        ->select(c | 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())
        ->asOrderedSet()]
    [if (abstractionSuppliers->notEmpty())]
      together {
      [for (contextClass : uml::Class | abstractionSuppliers)]
        [if (contextClass.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [contextClass.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10>' + contextClass.package.name + ':\\n')/]
      [/for]
      }
    [/if]
  [/let]
  
  ' Remaining context classes (excluding direct associated and abstraction suppliers).
  [for (contextClass : uml::Class |
      aClass.u_contextClasses()
        - aClass.eInverse(uml::Abstraction)->asSequence()
            ->collect(temp8 | temp8.supplier)
            ->collect(temp9 | temp9.oclAsType(uml::Class))
            ->asOrderedSet()
        - (aClass.u_associatedClasses() - aClass.superClass)
            ->sortedBy(temp10 | temp10.package.name)
            ->sortedBy(temp11 | temp11.name))]
    [let inSubset2 : Boolean = (aSubsetPackage <> null and aSubsetPackage.u_childDependencySupplierClasses()->includes(contextClass)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())]
      [if (inSubset2)][if (contextClass.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [contextClass.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10>' + contextClass.package.name + ':\\n')/][/if]
    [/let]
  [/for]
  
  ' Associations of the focal class.
  [for (anAssociation : uml::Association | aClass.u_associations())]
    [if (anAssociation.u_isAssociationInSubset(aClass, aSubsetPackage))]
      [if (aClass <> anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().type)]
        [let srcClass : uml::Classifier = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().type.oclAsType(uml::Classifier)]
          [let aggKind : String = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().aggregation.pu_aggregationKind()]
            [let tooltip : String = ' <U+2022> ' + anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName() + ':\\n' + anAssociation.u_commentBody()]
              [aClass.qualifiedName/] <-['['/]#grey]-[aggKind/] [srcClass.qualifiedName/] ['#'.pu_link(tooltip)/] : [anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName()/]
            [/let]
          [/let]
        [/let]
      [else]
        [let tgtClass : uml::Classifier = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().getOtherEnd().type.oclAsType(uml::Classifier)]
          [let aggKind : String = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().getOtherEnd().aggregation.pu_aggregationKind()]
            [let tooltip : String = ' <U+2022> ' + anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName() + ':\\n' + anAssociation.u_commentBody()]
              [aClass.qualifiedName/] [aggKind/]-['['/]#grey]-> [tgtClass.qualifiedName/] ['#'.pu_link(tooltip)/] : [anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName()/]
            [/let]
          [/let]
        [/let]
      [/if]
    [/if]
  [/for]
  
  [if (aClass.superClass->notEmpty())]
    ' Superclass hierarchy
    [aClass.pu_superClass(aClass, aSubsetPackage)/]
  [/if]
  [if (aClass.u_subClasses()->notEmpty())]
    ' Subclass hierarchy
    [aClass.pu_subClasses(aSubsetPackage)/]
  [/if]
  
  ' Abstraction relationships
  [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() and aClass.u_model().u_allAbstractionClients()->includes(aClass))]
    [for (anAbstraction : uml::Abstraction | aClass.eInverse(uml::Abstraction))]
        [aClass.qualifiedName/] .....> [anAbstraction.supplier->asSequence()->collect(temp16 | temp16.oclAsType(uml::Classifier))->collect(temp17 | temp17.qualifiedName)/] : [anAbstraction.abstractionType()/] 
    [/for]
  [/if]
  [if (aClass.u_model().u_allAbstractionSuppliers()->includes(aClass))]
    [for (anAbstraction : uml::Abstraction | aClass.eInverse(uml::Abstraction))]
        [aClass.qualifiedName/] <..... [anAbstraction.client->asSequence()->collect(temp18 | temp18.oclAsType(uml::Classifier))->collect(temp19 | temp19.qualifiedName)/] : [anAbstraction.abstractionType()/] 
    [/for]
  [/if]
  @enduml[/template]

[**
Generates a PlantUML context diagram for a UML data type.

The diagram shows:
  - The focal data type (highlighted) with its own attributes
  - Classes and data types that use this type as an attribute type,
    grouped by package, with dotted usage connections
  - Supertype inheritance hierarchy (via pu_superDataType)
  - Subtype inheritance hierarchy (via pu_subDataTypes)
  - Abstraction relationships

Attribute inclusion and usage connections are subject to subset
filtering via u_subsetDataTypeAttributes.

@param aDataType - The UML data type for which the diagram is generated.
/]
[template public pu_dataTypeDiagram(aDataType : uml::DataType)]
  @startuml
  [aDataType.pu_generationMessageDoc()/]
  left to right direction
  [aDataType.pu_options()/]
  
  title UML Diagram: [aDataType.eClass().name/] [aDataType.name/] in Context\n
  [let url : String = '../' + aDataType.u_path() + '.html']
    [let label : String =
        aDataType.u_model().u_modelTitle()
        + ' (' + aDataType.u_model().u_modelAcronym() + ') '
        + aDataType.u_model().u_modelMajorVersion()
        + '.' + aDataType.u_model().u_modelMinorVersion()
        + ' - ' + aDataType.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()]
      <style>
      title { FontSize: 20 }
      footer { hyperlinkUnderlineThickness 0 }
      </style>
      footer \n\n[url.pu_linkWithLabel(label)/]
    [/let]
  [/let]
  
  
  legend top right
  **Hint(s)**
  <color:grey>- The use of the data type is represented here by a dotted line (not formal UML).
  [if (aDataType.u_allSuperDataTypes()->notEmpty() or aDataType.u_allSubDataTypes()->notEmpty())]
    <color:grey>- The arrows of the inheritance tree are <color:['uml-diagram-inheritance-arrow-color'.getPropertyValue()/]>colored<color:grey>.
  [/if]
  endlegend
  
  ' Core data type of diagram
  [if (aDataType.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [aDataType.pu_classifierNameWithLabel('black', '<size:10> \\n')/] \
    ['uml-diagram-class-emphasis-color'.getPropertyValue()/] {
  [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | aDataType.ownedAttribute->select(temp20 | temp20.association = null))]
    [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() or aDataType.name.u_subsetDataTypeAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name))]
        [anAttribute.name/] : [anAttribute.type.pu_typeWithLink()/]
    [/if]
  [/for]
  }
  
  ' Data type definitions in own package
  [for (contextClassifier : uml::Classifier | aDataType.u_contextClassesOrDataTypes()->select(temp22 | temp22.package = aDataType.package))]
    [if (contextClassifier.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [contextClassifier.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10> \\n')/] {
    [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | contextClassifier.attribute->select(temp21 | temp21.association = null))]
      [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() or contextClassifier.name.u_subsetDataTypeAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name))]
          [anAttribute.name/] : [if (aDataType = anAttribute.type)][anAttribute.type.name/][else][anAttribute.type.pu_typeWithLink()/][/if]
      [/if]
    [/for]
    }
  [/for]
  
  ' Data type definitions in other packages
  [for (aPackage : uml::Package | aDataType.u_contextPackages())]
    [for (contextClassifier : uml::Classifier | aDataType.u_contextClassesOrDataTypes()->select(temp24 | temp24.package = aPackage))]
        [if (contextClassifier.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [contextClassifier.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10><color:grey>' + contextClassifier.package.name + ':\\n')/] {
      [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | contextClassifier.attribute->select(temp23 | temp23.association = null))]
        [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() or contextClassifier.name.u_subsetDataTypeAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name))]
            [anAttribute.name/] : [if (aDataType = anAttribute.type)][anAttribute.type.name/][else][anAttribute.type.pu_typeWithLink()/][/if]
        [/if]
      [/for]
      }
    [/for]
  [/for]
  
  ' Usage connections (dotted lines, non-formal UML)
  together {
  [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | aDataType.u_dataTypeUseProperties())]
    [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() or aDataType.name.u_subsetDataTypeAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name))]
        [anAttribute.owner.oclAsType(uml::Classifier).qualifiedName/]::[anAttribute.name/] ---- [aDataType.qualifiedName/] #grey;line.dotted;
    [/if]
  [/for]
  }
  
  [if (aDataType.general->notEmpty())]
    ' Supertype hierarchy
    [aDataType.pu_superDataType()/]
  [/if]
  [if (aDataType.u_subDataTypes()->notEmpty())]
    ' Subtype hierarchy
    [aDataType.pu_subDataTypes()/]
  [/if]
  
  ' Abstraction relationships
  together {
  [if (aDataType.u_model().u_allAbstractionClients()->includes(aDataType))]
    [for (anAbstraction : uml::Abstraction | aDataType.eInverse(uml::Abstraction))]
        [aDataType.qualifiedName/] .....> [anAbstraction.supplier->asSequence()->collect(temp25 | temp25.oclAsType(uml::Classifier))->collect(temp26 | temp26.qualifiedName)/] : [anAbstraction.abstractionType()/] 
    [/for]
  [/if]
  [if (aDataType.u_model().u_allAbstractionSuppliers()->includes(aDataType))]
    [for (anAbstraction : uml::Abstraction | aDataType.eInverse(uml::Abstraction))]
        [aDataType.qualifiedName/] <..... [anAbstraction.client->asSequence()->collect(temp27 | temp27.oclAsType(uml::Classifier))->collect(temp28 | temp28.qualifiedName)/] : [anAbstraction.abstractionType()/] 
    [/for]
  [/if]
  }
  @enduml[/template]

[**
Returns the PlantUML stereotype label for a UML abstraction,
derived from the abstraction's name:
  contains 'derivesFrom' -> <<Derive>>
  contains 'refines'     -> <<Refine>>
  contains 'tracesTo'    -> <<Trace>>

@param anAbstraction - A UML Abstraction relationship.
/]
[template public abstractionType(anAbstraction : uml::Abstraction)]
  [if (anAbstraction.name.contains('derivesFrom'))]
    <U+00AB>Derive<U+00BB>
  [elseif (anAbstraction.name.contains('refines'))]
    <U+00AB>Refine<U+00BB>
  [elseif (anAbstraction.name.contains('tracesTo'))]
    <U+00AB>Trace<U+00BB>
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Renders the superclass hierarchy for the focal class in a context
diagram. For each direct superclass (subject to subset filtering):

  1. Emits a note if the superclass has more than maxInherited
     associations, stating how many are shown.
  2. Iterates up to maxInherited inherited associations of the
     superclass (via u_limitedAssociations), rendering each as a
     PlantUML association arrow using u_isAssociationInSubset for
     subset filtering and u_commentBody for the tooltip.
  3. Renders the superclass node with its attributes.
  4. Emits the generalization arrow.
  5. Recurses upward via pu_superClass.

The maximum number of inherited associations shown per superclass
is controlled by the let binding 'maxInherited'. This local cap
prevents diagrams from becoming unreadable when a superclass has
many associations.

@param aClass     - The class whose superclasses are being rendered.
@param mainClass     - The original focal class at the root of the
                        recursion, passed through unchanged to allow
                        u_limitedAssociations to exclude the focal
                        class's own direct associations.
@param aSubsetPackage - The profile sub-package, or null for universe.
/]
[template public pu_superClass(aClass : uml::Class, mainClass : uml::Class, aSubsetPackage : uml::Package)]
  [for (aSuperClass : uml::Class | aClass.superClass->select(c | (aSubsetPackage <> null and aSubsetPackage.u_childDependencySupplierClasses()->includes(c)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())))]
    ' Associations of superclass [aSuperClass.name/]
    [let maxInherited : Integer = 3]
      [let limitedAssocs : OrderedSet(uml::Association) = aSuperClass.u_limitedAssociations(aClass)]
        [let showCount : Integer = if limitedAssocs->size() > maxInherited then maxInherited else limitedAssocs->size() endif]
          [if (limitedAssocs->size() > maxInherited)]
            note left of [aSuperClass.qualifiedName/] : Class has [aSuperClass.u_associations()->size()/] associations.\nOnly [maxInherited/] are shown here.
          [/if]
          [if (showCount > 0)]
            [for (anAssociation : uml::Association | limitedAssocs->subOrderedSet(1, showCount))]
              [if (anAssociation.u_isAssociationInSubset(aSuperClass, aSubsetPackage))]
                [if (aSuperClass <> anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().type)]
                  [let srcClass : uml::Classifier = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().type.oclAsType(uml::Classifier)]
                    [let aggKind : String = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().aggregation.pu_aggregationKind()]
                      [let tooltip : String = ' <U+2022> ' + anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName() + ':\\n' + anAssociation.u_commentBody()]
                        [aSuperClass.qualifiedName/] <-['['/]#grey][aggKind/] [srcClass.qualifiedName/] ['#'.pu_link(tooltip)/] : <U+2003>[anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName()/]
                      [/let]
                    [/let]
                  [/let]
                [else]
                  [let tgtClass : uml::Classifier = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().getOtherEnd().type.oclAsType(uml::Classifier)]
                    [let aggKind : String = anAssociation.ownedEnd->first().getOtherEnd().aggregation.pu_aggregationKind()]
                      [let tooltip : String = ' <U+2022> ' + anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName() + ':\\n' + anAssociation.u_commentBody()]
                        [aSuperClass.qualifiedName/] [aggKind/]-['['/]#grey]> [tgtClass.qualifiedName/] ['#'.pu_link(tooltip)/] : <U+2003>[anAssociation.u_shortAssociationName()/]
                      [/let]
                    [/let]
                  [/let]
                [/if]
              [/if]
            [/for]
          [/if]
        [/let]
      [/let]
    [/let]
    
    [if (aSuperClass.isAbstract)]abstract [/if]class [aSuperClass.pu_elementWithLink('blue', '<size:10> \\n')/] ['uml-diagram-package-default-color'.getPropertyValue()/] {
    [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | aSuperClass.ownedAttribute->select(temp33 | temp33.association = null)->select(a | (aSubsetPackage <> null and a.u_isAttributeInProfile(aSuperClass, aSubsetPackage)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and (aClass.name.u_subsetClassAttributes()->includes(a.name) or 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())))->sortedBy(a | a.name))]
        [anAttribute.name/] : [anAttribute.type.pu_typeWithLink()/]
    [/for]
    }
    
    [aSuperClass.qualifiedName/] <|-['['/]#D2691E]- [aClass.qualifiedName/]
    [aSuperClass.pu_superClass(mainClass, aSubsetPackage)/]
  [/for]
[/template]

[**
Renders supertype inheritance for a data type context diagram.
For each direct supertype, emits usage connections (dotted lines)
for the supertype's limited-use properties, the inheritance arrow,
and recurses upward.

@param aDataType - The data type whose supertypes are being rendered.
/]
[template public pu_superDataType(aDataType : uml::DataType)]
  [for (aSuperDataType : uml::DataType | aDataType.general->asSequence()->collect(temp34 | temp34.oclAsType(uml::DataType)))]
    ' Supertype usage connections for [aSuperDataType.name/]
    [for (anAttribute : uml::Property | aSuperDataType.u_limitedDataTypeUseProperties())]
      [aSuperDataType.qualifiedName/] --up-- [anAttribute.owner.oclAsType(uml::Classifier).qualifiedName/]::[anAttribute.name/] #grey;line.dotted;
    [/for]
    
    [aSuperDataType.qualifiedName/] <|--r-- [aDataType.qualifiedName/] #D2691E
    [aSuperDataType.pu_superDataType()/]
  [/for]
[/template]

[**
Renders subclass inheritance arrows recursively for a class context
diagram. Each subclass is subject to subset filtering via
u_profileSubsetClasses when 'profiles' is true.
Recurses into each subclass's own subclasses.

@param aClass        - The class whose subclasses are being rendered.
@param aSubsetPackage - The profile sub-package, or null for universe.
/]
[template public pu_subClasses(aClass : uml::Class, aSubsetPackage : uml::Package)]
  [for (subClass : uml::Class | aClass.u_subClasses()->select(c | (aSubsetPackage <> null and aSubsetPackage.u_childDependencySupplierClasses()->includes(c)) or (aSubsetPackage = null and 'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue())))]
      [aClass.qualifiedName/] <|--['['/]['uml-diagram-inheritance-arrow-color'.getPropertyValue()/]]- [subClass.qualifiedName/] 
    [if (subClass.u_subClasses()->notEmpty())][subClass.pu_subClasses(aSubsetPackage)/][/if]
  [/for]
[/template]

[**
Renders subtype inheritance arrows recursively for a data type
context diagram. Recurses into each subtype's own subtypes.

@param aDataType - The data type whose subtypes are being rendered.
/]
[template public pu_subDataTypes(aDataType : uml::DataType)]
  [for (subDataType : uml::DataType | aDataType.u_subDataTypes())]
      [aDataType.qualifiedName/] <|-r-- [subDataType.qualifiedName/] ['uml-diagram-inheritance-arrow-color'.getPropertyValue()/] 
    [if (subDataType.u_subDataTypes()->notEmpty())][subDataType.pu_subDataTypes()/][/if]
  [/for]
[/template]

[**
Generates a table row in RST list-table format for a single class
or data type attribute. The row is subject to subset filtering.
Columns: attribute name, owning classifier reference, description,
type reference, multiplicity, and default value.

@param anAttribute  - The UML property (attribute) to render.
@param aClassifier  - The classifier owning the attribute's diagram.
/]
[template public rst_processAttributeInTable(anAttribute : uml::Property, aClassifier : uml::Classifier)]
  [if ('includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue() 
      or aClassifier.name.u_subsetDataTypeAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name)
      or aClassifier.name.u_subsetClassAttributes()->includes(anAttribute.name)
    )]
    [let attributeClassifier : uml::Classifier = anAttribute.u_parent().oclAsType(uml::Classifier)]
      * - [anAttribute.name/]
      [if (attributeClassifier = aClassifier)]
          - \- *own [aClassifier.eClass().name.toLower()/]* \-
      [else]
          - :ref:`[attributeClassifier.u_packageQualifiedName()/]<[attributeClassifier.qualifiedName/]>`
      [/if]
        -
         [anAttribute.u_commentBody().replaceAll('=', '')/]
        - [anAttribute.type.rst_refDataType()/] 
        - [anAttribute.u_docMultiplicity()/]
        - [anAttribute.default/]
    [/let]
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Generates a RST :ref: link for a UML type. UML primitive types
(Boolean, Integer, Real, String) are rendered as plain text;
all other types are rendered as a :ref: cross-reference.

@param aType - A UML type to reference.
/]
[template public rst_refDataType(aType : uml::Type) post(self.trim())]
  [if (aType.u_isUmlPrimitive())]
    [aType.name/]
  [else]
    :ref:`[aType.qualifiedName/]`
  [/if]
[/template]

[comment]
Dead variant of rst_refDataType kept for reference:
[template public rst_refDataType(aType : uml::Type) post(self.trim())]
  [if (aType.ancestors()->notEmpty())]
    :ref:`[aType.qualifiedName/]`
  [else]
    [aType.name/]
  [/if]
[/template]
[/comment]

[**
Generates a table row in RST list-table format for a single UML
association. Columns: target multiplicity, association predicate
(short name), source class reference with qualified name, source
multiplicity.

@param a      - The UML association to render.
@param indent - Indentation string to prepend to each RST list item.
/]
[template public rst_processAssociationInTable(a : uml::Association, indent : String)]
  [indent/]* - [a.memberEnd->last().u_docMultiplicity()/]
  [indent/]  - [a.u_shortAssociationName()/]
  [indent/]  - :ref:`[a.memberEnd->first().type.oclAsType(uml::Classifier).u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()/]<[a.memberEnd->first().type.qualifiedName/]>`
  [indent/]  - [a.memberEnd->first().u_docMultiplicity()/]
[/template]

[**
Generates a RST :ref: cross-reference for a class, using the
simple qualified classifier name as the visible label and the
fully qualified name as the reference target.

@param aClass - A UML class to cross-reference.
/]
[template public rst_simpleQualifiedClassNameReference(aClass : uml::Class)]
  :ref:`[aClass.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()/]<[aClass.qualifiedName/]>`[/template]

[**
Generates a RST :ref: cross-reference for a classifier, using the
simple qualified classifier name as the visible label and the
fully qualified name as the reference target.

@param aClassifier - A UML classifier to cross-reference.
/]
[template public rst_simpleQualifiedClassifierNameReference(aClassifier : uml::Classifier)]
  :ref:`[aClassifier.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()/]<[aClassifier.qualifiedName/]>`[/template]

[**
Generates a RST :ref: cross-reference for a class using only the
fully qualified name (no visible label override).

@param aClass - A UML class to cross-reference.
/]
[template public rst_classNameReference(aClass : uml::Class)]
  :ref:`[aClass.qualifiedName/]`[/template]

[**
Generates a RST :ref: cross-reference for a classifier using only
the fully qualified name (no visible label override).

@param aClassifier - A UML classifier to cross-reference.
/]
[template public rst_classifierNameReference(aClassifier : uml::Classifier)]
  :ref:`[aClassifier.qualifiedName/]`[/template]

[**
Renders a class name in RST, wrapping it in italic emphasis markers
when the class is abstract.

@param aClass - A UML class.
/]
[template public rst_className(aClass : uml::Class)]
  [if (aClass.isAbstract)]*[aClass.name/]*[else][aClass.name/][/if][/template]

[**
Injects RST :ref: cross-references into a documentation string for
every class in aClassSequence whose name appears as a word boundary
followed by punctuation in the string. Recurses through the sequence
one class at a time.

@param s              - The documentation string to process.
@param aClass         - The class being documented (excluded from
                        self-reference injection).
@param aClassSequence - The sequence of classes to inject as :ref:.
/]
[query public rst_addClassReferencesToDocumentation(s : String, aClass : uml::Class, aClassSequence : Sequence(uml::Class)) : String = if aClassSequence->size() = 0 then s else if aClassSequence->first() <> aClass then s.replaceAll('(\\s)'.concat(aClassSequence->first().name.concat('([\\.,\\s])')), '$1'.concat(aClassSequence->first().rst_classNameReference().concat('$2'))).rst_addClassReferencesToDocumentation(aClass, aClassSequence->excluding(aClassSequence->first())) else s.rst_addClassReferencesToDocumentation(aClass, aClassSequence->excluding(aClassSequence->first())) endif endif/]

[**
Post-processing template that prefixes every non-empty line of a
multi-line string with a fixed number of spaces. Used to produce
RST-indented include blocks when a generated diagram is embedded
in an RST file.

@param s            - The string to indent.
@param indentAmount - The number of leading spaces to add per line.
/]
[template public e_indent(s : String, indentAmount : Integer)]
  [let blanks : String = '                                        ']
    [s.replaceAll('(.+)', blanks.first(indentAmount) + '$1')/]
  [/let]
[/template]

[**
Post-processing template that inserts a fixed indentation string
after every newline character in a string. Complementary to e_indent
for use within a string value rather than on block boundaries.

@param s      - The string to indent.
@param indent - The number of leading spaces to insert after each
                newline.
/]
[template public e_indent2(s : String, indent : Integer)]
  [let blanks : String = '                                        ']
    [s.replaceAll('\n', '\n' + blanks.first(indent))/]
  [/let]
[/template]

[**
Generates the RST inheritance tree section for a classifier,
rendered as a collapsible dropdown. The tree shows all superclass
ancestors from the root downward to the focal class, followed by
all direct and indirect subclasses.

When the classifier has superclasses, the root ancestor appears
first without indentation and each subsequent ancestor is indented
by 4 em-spaces per level, with the focal class shown in :focus:.
When the classifier has no superclasses but does have subclasses,
only the focal class and its subtree are shown.

@param aClassifier - The UML classifier for which the inheritance
                     tree is generated.
/]
[template public rst_classOrDataTypeInheritance(aClassifier : uml::Classifier)]
  Inheritance
  ===========
  
  .. dropdown:: Inheritance
     :class-container: inheritance-dropdown
  
     .. |_| unicode:: U+2003 .. em space
  
     .. role:: focus
  
  [let indent : String = '|_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| |_| ']
    [if (aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->notEmpty())]
      [let nSuperClasses : Integer = aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->size()]
           [if (aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->last().isAbstract)].. cssclass:: abstract[else].. cssclass:: regular[/if]
        
           | [aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->last().rst_simpleQualifiedClassifierNameReference()/]
        
        [for (aSuperClassifier : uml::Classifier | aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->excluding(aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->last())->reverse())]
             [if (aSuperClassifier.isAbstract)].. cssclass:: abstract[else].. cssclass:: regular[/if]
          
             | [indent.first(aClassifier.u_allSuperClassifiers()->indexOf(aSuperClassifier) * 4)/]ᐊ── [aSuperClassifier.rst_simpleQualifiedClassifierNameReference()/]
          
        [/for]
           [if (aClassifier.isAbstract)].. cssclass:: abstract[else].. cssclass:: regular[/if]
        
           | [indent.first(nSuperClasses * 4)/]ᐊ── :focus:`[aClassifier.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()/]`
        
        [aClassifier.rst_subClasses(indent.first((nSuperClasses + 1) * 4))/]
      [/let]
    [elseif (aClassifier.u_subClassesOrSubDataTypes()->notEmpty())]
         [if (aClassifier.isAbstract)].. cssclass:: abstract[else].. cssclass:: regular[/if]
      
         | :focus:`[aClassifier.u_simpleQualifiedClassifierName()/]`
      
      [aClassifier.rst_subClasses('   ')/]
    [/if]
  [/let]
[/template]

[**
Generates a recursive RST subclass/subtype list for the inheritance
tree dropdown. Each entry is rendered with appropriate CSS class
(abstract or regular) and indented by the given indent string.
Recurses into each child's own subtree.

When 'profiles' is true, only subclasses/subtypes that are members
of the dependency-defined profile subset are shown (checked by object
identity via u_profileSubsetClasses for classes and
u_profileSubsetDataTypes for data types). When 'includeAllItems' is
true, all subclasses and subtypes are shown regardless of the subset.

@param aClassifier - The classifier whose children are listed.
@param indent      - The current indentation prefix string.
/]
[template public rst_subClasses(aClassifier : uml::Classifier, indent : String)]
  [for (c : uml::Classifier | aClassifier.u_subClassesOrSubDataTypes()
      ->select(sub |
        'includeAllItems'.isPropertyTrue()
        or (sub.oclIsKindOf(uml::Class)
            and aClassifier.u_profileSubsetClasses()->includes(sub.oclAsType(uml::Class)))
        or (sub.oclIsKindOf(uml::DataType)
            and aClassifier.u_profileSubsetDataTypes()->includes(sub.oclAsType(uml::DataType)))))]
       [if (c.isAbstract)].. cssclass:: abstract[else].. cssclass:: regular[/if]
    
       | [indent/]ᐊ── [c.rst_simpleQualifiedClassifierNameReference()/]
    
    [if (c.u_subClassesOrSubDataTypes()->notEmpty())][c.rst_subClasses(indent.concat('|_| '))/][/if]
  [/for]
[/template]

[**
Generates the opening HTML markup for the SVG diagram modal
container. The modal allows the diagram to be enlarged and
pan/zoomed in the browser. Must be paired with diagramModalPostCode.

@param anOclAny - Any EObject; used only as receiver for dispatch.
/]
[template public diagramModalPreCode(anOclAny : ecore::EObject)]
  <div id="svgDiagram">
    <span id="openModal" class="noprint" title="Enlarge diagram">&#x2922;</span>[/template]

[**
Generates the closing HTML markup for the SVG diagram modal,
including the modal overlay, pan/zoom controls, and download buttons
for PNG and SVG export.

@param anOclAny - Any EObject; used only as receiver for dispatch.
/]
[template public diagramModalPostCode(anOclAny : ecore::EObject)]
  </div>
  <div id="myModal" class="modal">
    <!-- Modal content -->
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div id="buttons">
        <span id="resetDiagram" title="Reset pan/zoom">&circlearrowleft;</span>
        <div class="dropdown dropdown-download-buttons">
          <span id="downloadDiagram" title="Download diagram"  data-bs-toggle="dropdown" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Download diagram">&DownArrowBar;</span>
          <ul class="dropdown-menu">
            <li>
              <span id="downloadDiagramPng" title="Download diagram as PNG">
                <span class="btn__icon-container">
                  <svg class="svg-inline--fa fa-file" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="file" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 384 512" data-fa-i2svg="">
                    <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 64C0 28.7 28.7 0 64 0H224V128c0 17.7 14.3 32 32 32H384V448c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V64zm384 64H256V0L384 128z"></path>
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <span class="btn__text-container">Download as PNG</span>
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span id="downloadDiagramSvg" title="Download diagram as SVG">
                <span class="btn__icon-container">
                  <svg class="svg-inline--fa fa-file" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="file" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 384 512" data-fa-i2svg="">
                    <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 64C0 28.7 28.7 0 64 0H224V128c0 17.7 14.3 32 32 32H384V448c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V64zm384 64H256V0L384 128z"></path>
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <span class="btn__text-container">Download as SVG</span>
              </span>
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <span id="closeModal" title="Close diagram view">&#x2715;</span>
      </div>
      <div id="panzoom-wrapper">
        <div id="panzoom-area">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>[/template]
